  "title": "Heights compute the transfer between a split point and any line",
  "subject": "How to compute, without enumeration, which port patterns and gluing-line patterns occur together in a plane piece",
  "conclusion": "In a point split of a plane knot space the solutions are corner matchings, and which pairs of port patterns and gluing-line patterns occur together is decided exactly by heights: fix the line's corner, project the difference constraints onto six regions by shortest paths, and test parities by halving. This makes the halo computable on plane pieces of hundreds of points, and it matched enumeration on all 1,221 small cases.",
